    "name": "High-Altitude Passive Solar Shelter — Ladakh Optimized",
    "description": "Full-featured shelter designed for extreme cold at 4200m altitude near Pangong Tso, Ladakh. Features: 450mm rammed earth walls for thermal mass, 150mm XPS insulation, large south-facing double-low-e windows, internal water wall for thermal storage, minimal north openings, tight construction, south overhang for summer shading. Orientation 180° (south-facing). This represents the target design for the DRDO problem statement.",
